      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A variation on this request would be changing the label for the related game object from 'This' to 'gameObject' or something similar. Then create a new node for the UdonBehavior reference and call it 'This'.\nThat would bring the naming more in line with what is generally expected from a developer standpoint and can help bridge a small bit of confusion when inter-oping between Graph and community created compilers (such as usharp).",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-07-17T22:11:32.038Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For consistency with existing graph nodes like Const <Primitive>, Const Null and Const This, please also add an explicit node for the currently executing script, maybe like Const UdonBehavior.\nThis will also help alleviate some confusion on how to access the current script's own reference within the script itself. There are a few ways to acquire the reference, but for newer creators it's much less intuitive than the well known node search method.",
